  "scope": "T03 finite scalar captured target analysis admission/preparation/execution and native/Python APIs. Not actual editor integration, recorder replay, full-family certification, macOS or release readiness.",
  "implementation": [
    "Metadata-only estimates reuse target histogram/mask/record admission and bounded metadata matching, with added encoded/typed calibration, one lookup, kernel/median scratch, retained per-plane rows and simultaneous plot allowance.",
    "Immutable source/target/options/limits/effective values; serial one-read-per-plane execution preserves C/Z/T/ROI membership and explicit order. Profile-only targets retain non-area selection guards without rasterization.",
    "Statistics and thin straight-line values reuse existing numerical kernels; shared physical distance axis uses the captured affine. Finite-policy UInt8/UInt16/Float32 only; other variants remain in the roadmap.",
    "Existing execution scopes provide cancellation/checkpoints and exception disposal. Detached output retains no provider; source/global/membership validation remains mandatory for owner-controlled UI adoption. No document/history edit or new controller.",
    "Lookup decoding once per preparation and shared Python statistics formatter eliminate repeated work. Effective records are built directly rather than temporarily copying displaced local calibration strings; existing sampling estimates already conservatively charged that copy, so no cap violation is asserted."
  ],
